{
  "sub_hypo": [
    {
      "text": "Among Black NLSY79 respondents, incarceration during 1985–1994 is associated with lower wealth growth from 1985 to 1996, with a wealth-growth penalty that widens monotonically across increasing 1985 wealth tiers.",
      "context": "Black respondents (race=black, N=3,013; 159 ever jailed) in a 12,013-row complete-case extract. Income is absent; 1985 composite wealth is a labelled proxy for income strata: ≤$0, >$0–$10,000, and >$10,000. Associations are not causal: incarceration selection is non-random and sex-confounded; only 16 ever-jailed Black respondents are female, with female × tier × incarceration cells of approximately 3–13. Incarceration excludes spells before 1985 and after 1994; the extract hides non-random panel attrition. No IPW, IV, matching, or DiD is applied.",
