      "relations": "Ever-jailed respondents' mean wealth falls from $29,906 in 1985 to $23,115 in 1996 (reported change −$6,792), whereas never-jailed peers gain $49,266. The bootstrap median jailed-minus-never-jailed growth gap is −$16,600 (CI [−$28,051, −$1,804], excluding zero); the sex-adjusted OLS mean gap is −$60,141. These are the largest tier-specific penalties, interpreted associationally."
